      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But it displeased Jonah exceedingly, and he was angry. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.34.6"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 34.6",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": ".",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And he prayed to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and said, “I pray thee, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", is not this what I said when I was yet in my country? That is why I made haste to flee to Tarshish; for I knew that thou art a gracious God and merciful, slow to anger, and abounding in steadfast love, and repentest of evil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore now, O ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", take my life from me, I beseech thee, for it is better for me to die than to live.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said, “Do you do well to be angry?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Jonah went out of the city and sat to the east of the city, and made a booth for himself there. He sat under it in the shade, till he should see what would become of the city.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " God appointed a plant,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.6",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "qiqayon,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "probably",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the castor oil plant",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and made it come up over Jonah, that it might be a shade over his head, to save him from his discomfort. So Jonah was exceedingly glad because of the plant.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.6",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "qiqayon,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "probably",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the castor oil plant",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when dawn came up the next day, God appointed a worm which attacked the plant,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.7",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "qiqayon,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "probably",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the castor oil plant",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " so that it withered. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the sun rose, God appointed a sultry east wind, and the sun beat upon the head of Jonah so that he was faint; and he asked that he might die, and said, “It is better for me to die than to live.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But God said to Jonah, “Do you do well to be angry for the plant?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.9",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "qiqayon,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "probably",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the castor oil plant",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " And he said, “I do well to be angry, angry enough to die.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said, “You pity the plant,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.10",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "qiqayon,",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "probably",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the castor oil plant",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " for which you did not labor, nor did you make it grow, which came into being in a night, and perished in a night. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JON 4:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And should not I pity Nineveh, that great city, in which there are more than a hundred and twenty thousand persons who do not know their right hand from their left, and also much cattle?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JON.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JON.4.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
